  "problem": "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t.$",
  "worked_solution": "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\frac{1}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-{t}^{-1}) \\\\  & =1-(-{t}^{-2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
